Later views of the Greek and Egyptian pantheons fit NetHack better.
Thoth has come to symbolize or rule magic, especially among occultists.
Hermes developed a close link to medicine through his connection with
alchemists, and today many use his staff as a symbol of medicine.
(Occultism can justify this by pointing to the importance of
Thoth-Hermes and Wisdom in the creation of Apollo's Sun. The priests of
Thoth gave him a similar role. The Norse bards, who call Odin the chief
of the gods, served Odin.) I never encountered Anhur's name before
NetHack, and I don't know how the DevTeam chose him. But it turns out
that two degrees of separation takes you from Anhur to Discordianism:
Anhur->Horus->Thelema->Disco



